[statement]
A dependency gives way to a provider needing it, chosen for a name
packages only provide, where another package could answer that name
(`a-dependency-gives-way-to-a-choice-needing-it`): `a` needs `w`, which
`c` 3 and `d` 1 provide; `c` 3 needs `f`, and `f` 3, the best candidate
for `f`, forbids `w`. apk takes `c` 3 and `f` 2. Contrast
`a-dependency-does-not-give-way-to-the-one-provider-of-a-name-needing-it`.

[repository]
P:f
V:3
D:!w

P:a
V:3
D:w

P:c
V:3
D:f
p:w=1

P:d
V:1
p:w=1

P:f
V:2

[request]
a

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install f 2
install c 3
install a 3
